cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use greek-conversion in research or in a published resource, please
  cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: greek-conversion
abstract: >-
  A TypeScript library for bidirectional conversion between Greek, Beta Code,
  and scientific transliteration. It defines atomic conversion options,
  implements published conventions (ALA-LC, BnF, ISO 843, SBL, TLG, Perseus)
  as presets over those options, and reports the information a conversion
  loses.
authors:
  - family-names: Boquet
    given-names: Antoine
version: 1.0.0-rc.5
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/defense-humanites/greek-conversion"
url: "https://defense-humanites.github.io/greek-conversion/"
keywords:
  - Ancient Greek
  - Modern Greek
  - polytonic Greek
  - Beta Code
  - transliteration
  - romanization
  - digital humanities
